Q: What conditions must be met to receive the spend‑bonus interest and which Horizon Card transactions are excluded?
A: - Complete at least five qualifying Horizon Card purchases of {{faq_321e86c6_001}} or more each within the calendar month. Meeting this threshold activates the spend‑bonus on your deposit balance up to {{faq_321e86c6_002}} for that month. The transactions must be posted in the same month to be counted.
- The following card activities do **not** satisfy the eligibility criteria:
  - Using the Horizon Card as an ATM or EFTPOS cash‑withdrawal function;
  - Transferring balances to the Horizon Card;
  - Paying online bills directly from your savings account;
  - Repaying loans, credit facilities, or other deposit accounts;
  - Adding value to any stored‑value product;
  - Settling bills at AXS terminals with your savings account;
  - Any fees or charges applied to the Horizon Card (annual fees, interest, administrative fees, cash‑advance fees, finance charges, late‑payment penalties, etc.);
  - Outstanding balances carried over from previous months;
  - Transactions linked to betting or gambling;
  - Any other card charges that Horizon Bank may deem ineligible from time to time.
- Both the base interest and the bonus interest are calculated daily on a {{faq_321e86c6_003}}‑day year basis.

